From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:57:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: put the OCI of the sending link into an EAPOL-Key
 frame

The authenticator of a non-AP MLD runs on the association link. It puts
the OCI of that link into EAPOL-Key message 3/4, and validates message
2/4 and group message 2/2 against that link. hostapd sends these frames
on the link that an established advertised TID-to-link mapping enables,
and to an authorized non-AP MLD on a link that the driver picks. The
station can answer on any link. Group message 1/2 to a non-AP MLD
carries no OCI KDE at all, so a station with OCV refuses it with "did
not receive mandatory OCI".

IEEE Std 802.11-2024 12.7.6.1: "OCI KDE contains the current operating
channel information for the operating channel in which the EAPOL-Key PDU
is sent"; 12.7.7.1: "The OCI represents the current operating channel
information using which the EAPOL-Key PDU is sent". IEEE Std
802.11be-2024 12.2.10 names "the link used for the establishment of a
security association". That a group message validates on its receive
link follows from the 12.7.7.1 wording, not from 12.2.10.

Put the OCI of the link that sends the frame into EAPOL-Key message 3/4
and into group message 1/2, also for a non-AP MLD. Validate a received
OCI against the channel of the link that received the frame and the
capabilities of the station on that link. With OCV, send the EAPOL-Key
frames of an authorized non-AP MLD on that link as well, since their OCI
names it. A frame with no receive link falls back to the association
link.

While here, validate the OCI of an SA Query frame with the capabilities
of the station on the link that received it, as the channel already is.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
